      "pg_account": {
        "eyebrow_html": "My glass railing project",
        "heading_html": "Your glass railing project, all in one place",
        "text_html": "Sign in to track your order, follow the step-by-step install checklist, find your local building code and keep your warranty handy.",
        "signin_label_html": "Sign in",
        "steps_eyebrow_html": "Step by step",
        "steps_heading_html": "Installation checklist",
        "tools_html": "Measuring tape\nLevel (magnetic)\nPencil and chalk line\nPower drill with 1/8\" and 5/16\" bits\nAllen key\nWrench",
        "care_html": "Glass: a soft cloth and a non-abrasive glass cleaner. Skip scouring pads and razor blades.\nHardware: rinse with fresh water a few times a year, more often near pools or salt water.\nEach spring: check the clamps and cap rail and re-tighten anything loose.\nWinter: use a plastic shovel near the glass and rinse off de-icing salt.",
        "refer_title_html": "Love your railing?",
        "refer_text_html": "Refer friends and neighbours through our affiliate program and earn on every order they place.",
        "refer_button_html": "Join the program",
        "videos_heading_html": "Video guides",
        "recommend_heading_html": "Complete your railing",
        "steps1_html": "Mark the glass line | Snap a chalk line where the glass will stand.\nLay out panels and gaps | Mark each panel with a 1\" gap between panels (3/4\" to 2\" works).\nMark the spigot positions | About 25% of the glass length in from each edge.\nDrill the anchor holes | Use the spigot as a template and stay on the chalk line.\nFasten the spigots | Screw them down, keeping each one on the line.\nLevel the spigots | Check each spigot is straight with a magnetic level.\nSet the glass | A two-person job: lower each panel into its spigots.",
        "steps2_html": "Match the panel heights | Bring every panel level with the tallest one.\nSquare up the angles | Start from the corners and align each panel.\nFit the clamps | Usually about 6\" below the top of the glass.\nInstall the cap rail | Clean the edge, seat the gasket and press the rail on.\nHang the gate | Mount the hinges and latch.\nAdd the gate lock | Fit it on the outside with the recommended spacing."
      },
